course: dictionary
lesson: 5998
title: Measure: a tool and a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To measure something is to find out how big, long, heavy, hot or hot or how much of it there is, using a tool such as a ruler, tape, scales or clock. Here measure is a verb: you measure, you measure out, you are measuring.
explain: «It measures 5 cm» tells you the size of something. Measures means "is exactly this long", because someone found the length with a tool. Ask yourself: what tool would I use? A ruler for length, scales for weight, a clock for time.
explain: Read the words around measure. «The longest reliably measured reticulated pythons were about 7 metres, though stories claim far more.» The word reliably tells you the measured ones are checked, real numbers, while the stories are not.
explain: Measure is also a noun. A measure is an amount or a unit, like a cup or a metre. Measures can also be steps taken to do something, like «safety measures», which are actions to keep people safe.
fact: To measure means to find the size, length, weight, time or amount of something with a tool.
fact: «It measures 5 cm» tells you how big something is.
fact: A measure is an amount or a unit, like a cup or a metre.
fact: «Safety measures» are steps taken to keep people safe.
fact: In music, a measure is one short part of a tune, also called a bar.
exercise: «Longitude measures how far east or west a place is from the prime meridian.» What does measures mean here? | Paints a map of the sea | *Finds out how far east or west a place is | Makes a loud sound | Moves a place to Greenwich
exercise: Which tool would you use to measure weight? | A cup | A clock | A ruler | *Scales
exercise: In cooking, you measure flour with a cup. What is a cup in this sense? | A bar of a tune | A kind of knife | *A measure, an amount | A safety step
test: «Schools take safety measures.» What does measures mean here? | Amounts of water | Pieces of a tune | *Steps taken to keep people safe | Tools for finding size
test: In music, one short part of a tune is called what? | *A bar | A cup | A depth | A metre
exam: «The baker added a few raisins for good measure.» What does for good measure mean? | To check the size with a ruler | By weight only | To stop the cake from burning | *As a little extra
